{"text": "Walk back down the hall now, past the prints, past the robes, to the flat robe on its rack. Beck's thesis follows the furiso day at the coming of age day, but her definition is a general one. It covers the whole family you have just passed. The shape is the plain part. Unworn, a kimono is completely flat. No darts, no tucks, nothing to hold a body's form. The practice is the rest. A kimono maker, Yamaguchi Genbei, put a figure on it. Seventy percent of what makes a kimono a kimono is how it is worn. That is a maker's view, not a measurement, and the practice has a history. Laws on cloth under the shoguns. After the war, one book with three hundred and ninety rules. So the answer is both. A garment and a set of rules. Whichever you chose at the entrance, you are holding half of it. Becky adds one more thing. \"Rules can be bent,\" she writes, \"and clothes altered.\" The robe stays on its rack, flat, until someone puts it on. Thank you for walking with us.", "duration": 67.44, "timestamps": {"word": [{"word": "Walk", "start": 0.12, "end": 0.32}, {"word": "back", "start": 0.36, "end": 0.56}, {"word": "down", "start": 0.6, "end": 0.78}, {"word": "the", "start": 0.82, "end": 0.9}, {"word": "hall", "start": 0.94, "end": 1.14}, {"word": "now,", "start": 1.2, "end": 1.4}, {"word": "past", "start": 1.76, "end": 1.98}, {"word": "the", "start": 2.02, "end": 2.1}, {"word": "prints,", "start": 2.14, "end": 2.5}, {"word": "past", "start": 2.64, "end": 2.86}, {"word": "the", "start": 2.92, "end": 3}, {"word": "robes,", "start": 3.06, "end": 3.38}, {"word": "to", "start": 3.64, "end": 3.7}, {"word": "the", "start": 3.74, "end": 3.82}, {"word": "flat", "start": 3.88, "end": 4.1}, {"word": "robe", "start": 4.22, "end": 4.46}, {"word": "on", "start": 4.5, "end": 4.56}, {"word": "its", "start": 4.62, "end": 4.8}, {"word": "rack.", "start": 4.88, "end": 5.22}, {"word": "Beck's", "start": 5.94, "end": 6.24}, {"word": "thesis", "start": 6.3, "end": 6.7}, {"word": "follows", "st